  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Moserah and Moseroth are wilderness stations (Deuteronomy 10:6 and Numbers 33:30). Their derivation from a band is uncertain. Esarhaddon bears an Assyrian royal name and Esther’s longer name gives no evidence of this root. Neither is assigned here. The similar Syriac word for a copper coin in Matthew 10:29 is a loan corresponding to ἀσσάριον. The word for wood in the Aramaic index belongs to ets."
